    {
      "target": "u3",
      "focus": ["S"],
      "change": "Keep the direction of seeking unvisited locations and avoiding revisits, but widen the anti-revisit condition from only locations 'already shown to be empty' to any location already checked that did not contain the required object (a checked non-empty location that simply lacked the target also counts), and broaden 'unvisited containers' to unvisited locations including both closed containers and surfaces. Preserve the surface-reveals-contents clause and the requirement to search closed containers.",
      "reason": "Current evidence exposes a gap in the existing condition: `P2:10`, `P2:16`, `P2:20` and `P2:27` reopen fridge 1, which is not empty (it holds apples, cups, potatoes) but contains no bread, yet the clause as written forbids re-checking only locations 'already shown to be empty', so these repeated target-absent revisits are not covered and the run ends at the step limit without acquiring bread. Widening also matters because `P4:41` reached the target only by extending to diningtable 1, while `P6:37` found the plate by opening cabinet 9, supporting continued one-pass coverage of unvisited containers and surfaces. Historical `M2` reports a counterpart failure in which the candidate cycled among previously inspected fridge/countertop/cabinet/shelf/drawer locations and never reached a plausible surface (diningtable 1), and `M1` reports extended rechecking of already-inspected locations; both support widening the coverage expectation rather than narrowing it. The condition remains usable because a location's contents are shown in the current observation when reached, so 'did not contain the required object' is checkable without full-history tracking. This widens applicability rather than adding an exception.",
      "to": {
        "patch": "--- a/SKILL.md\n+++ b/SKILL.md\n@@\n- When the required object is not visible on surfaces reached so far, search closed containers by opening drawers and cabinets (and the fridge/microwave) and check shelves, moving to unvisited containers rather than re-checking locations already shown to be empty.\n- Countertops and diningtables reveal their contents directly when reached, so visit unvisited surfaces before returning to already-seen ones.\n+ When the required object is not visible on surfaces reached so far, search closed containers by opening drawers and cabinets (and the fridge/microwave) and check shelves, moving to unvisited locations\u2014containers as well as surfaces\u2014rather than re-checking any location already checked that did not contain the required object; prefer trying a location you have not yet checked over returning to one you have already checked.\n+ Countertops and diningtables reveal their contents directly when reached, so visit these unvisited surfaces before returning to already-seen ones.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "u4",
